# PeoplePay360 Boilerplate

Act as an Expert UI/UX Frontend Engineer. I need to build a boilerplate UI for "PeoplePay360" — an enterprise HR & Payroll application. 

CRITICAL CONSTRAINT: Do NOT implement any real API fetching, backend connections, or authentication (No Clerk, No Axios, No fetch). Use hardcoded mock data and React state to make the UI interactive. Focus 100% of your effort on making the UI look exactly like a native Odoo Enterprise (v18) application using Tailwind CSS, Lucide Icons, and Shadcn UI components.

======================================================================
1. ODOO DESIGN SYSTEM (TAILWIND CONFIG)
======================================================================
Inject these specific Odoo design tokens into the styling:
- Colors:
  * Primary Brand: #714B67 (Odoo Dirty Purple - use for primary buttons and focus rings)
  * Secondary Text: #1A1F36 (Headings)
  * Backgrounds: Base (#FFFFFF), Surface (#F8F9FA), Muted (#F1F3F4)
  * Semantic Badges: Success (#00C853), Warning (#FFB300), Danger (#FF1744)
- Typography:
  * Font: 'Inter', sans-serif. 
  * Headings must be bold (weight 700) with tight line-height. Use 12px for table headers, 14px for table cells, and 16px for body text to maintain high data density.
- Borders/Spacing: 
  * Use 4px rounding for inputs/buttons, 8px for cards, and full pill-rounding for status badges. 

======================================================================
2. THE APP SHELL (NAVIGATION)
======================================================================
Build a fixed top navigation bar:
- Left: Brand name "PeoplePay360" (bold, text-[#714B67]).
- Center/Left: Horizontal navigation links (Employees, Contracts, Attendance, Time Off, Payroll). Highlight "Contracts" as the active tab.
- Right: Search icon, Bell icon, and a dummy User Avatar circle.

======================================================================
3. SCREEN: CONTRACT MANAGEMENT (LIST VIEW)
======================================================================
Build the main content area as an Odoo-style high-density Data List.
- Action Bar (Top of page):
  * "New Contract" button (Primary purple button). Clicking this should open the Contract Form Modal.
  * Search input field.
  * Filter dropdown (All, Active, Draft).
- Data Table:
  * Create a clean, borderless table structure.
  * Columns: Checkbox, Contract Reference, Employee Name, Start Date, End Date, Wage, Status.
  * Mock Data: Populate the table with 4 mock rows.
  * Status Badges: Use pill-shaped badges. "Active" (Green background, white text), "Draft" (Amber background, dark text), "Expired" (Red background, white text).

======================================================================
4. MODAL: CONTRACT FORM (CREATE/EDIT)
======================================================================
When "New Contract" is clicked, open a beautifully styled Modal/Dialog.
- Header: "New Contract"
- Form Layout: Use an Odoo-style 2-column grid layout for fields.
- Fields (Use standard input components):
  * Employee (Select dropdown - mock a few names)
  * Contract Reference (Text input)
  * Start Date (Date input)
  * End Date (Date input)
  * Wage (Number input with currency symbol)
  * Pay Frequency (Select: Monthly, Bi-Weekly, Weekly)
  * Status (Select: Draft, Active)
- Footer Actions:
  * "Discard" (Neutral/Ghost button) - closes modal.
  * "Save" (Primary purple button) - closes modal and adds a dummy row to the table using React state.

Please generate this beautiful, interactive boilerplate now!

